After scoping out some places I wanted to try in Philadelphia for a work trip, Little Thai Market popped up. The reviews were raving about the salmon curry, which piqued my interest as I normally don't venture into seafood based curries. Upon arriving at the Reading Market, there was a long line in front that I was willing to stand in. They give you two options for your base on the curry dish, either rice with a garnish of broccoli, or all broccoli. I decided to go with the standard of all rice so I could let all the flavors come through the dish.

A very haggard employee took my order as he was helping to heat the salmon, grill the salmon, and fill the plates with orders. He came off as slightly rude, but I didn't hold this against him as he "}

{"aspect_id":"cleanliness","definition":"判断评论描述的餐厅、桌面、餐具或卫生间清洁程度。高分只表示更干净，低分只表示更脏。","relevance_scale":{"0":"评论没有谈到该特征","1":"只能从评论中间接、勉强推测该特征","2":"评论明确谈到该特征，但描述较短或上下文有限","3":"评论明确谈到该特征，并提供了清楚、充分的描述"},"strength_scale":{"0":"非常脏或不卫生，存在严重、具体的卫生问题","1":"比较脏，桌面、地面、餐具或卫生间有明显问题","2":"清洁程度一般、不同区域表现不一或处于普通水平","3":"比较干净，主要区域维护良好","4":"非常干净整洁，各区域卫生状况都很出色"},"special_rules":["装修陈旧不等于不干净，装修漂亮也不等于卫生良好。","只评价评论明确描述的卫生和清洁情况。"],"review_text":"Best breakfast place I have been to.

My girlfriend and I ate here after the philly marathon.  The place was packed and with good reason. The food is amazing.  My girlfriend got the canoli french toast while I went for the huevos rancheros.  Both were unbelievable.  We try to go every few weeks just to refresh our love for the place.  Plan on waiting 20-30 mins for a table though.  The place is this busy for a reason.

